{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"That can be true in limited circumstances, but purpose and impact matter. A private group exploring a specific European ancestry is different from an organization that excludes nonwhite people from jobs, housing, services, or political influence.\n\n“White people only” needs a stronger justification than shared cultural interest, because whiteness encompasses many distinct cultures. Relevant questions are whether the exclusion serves a legitimate need, whether inclusion would undermine that need, and whether the group promotes racial superiority or harms others. Apply those standards consistently across racial groups, while accounting for context."}}
